## Search terms / query-level data — **not available**

I have no search-terms report or query-level conversion data. I cannot name any top converting terms or keyword expansion opportunities. For context only (not performance evidence): one keyword change was applied 2026-11-01 to "Search - product terms" via prop-b1e2ede4 — "paid media analytics" (phrase), "ppc attribution" (phrase), "gtm tracking" (exact) — which is too recent to appear in the 30-day window anyway.

## Caveats

- **Conversion volume is modest** (28 → 42/wk; 131/30d), so week-over-week percentage moves are noisy; the CPA "flat" result is the robust signal, not the +50% conversions.
- Platform conversion definitions differ from other platforms and from warehouse outcomes — figures here are Google Ads platform-reported only.
- To answer your actual question, you'd need a per-campaign report from the Google Ads account plus warehouse qualified-lead/pipeline data joined at the campaign level.

